### 1.2 Cache Blocking & Loop Tiling

**Problem**: Column-major vs row-major memory access

```chapel
// BAD: Column-wise cache misses
for j in 0..#N do
  for i in 0..#N do
    C[i,j] += A[i,k] * B[k,j];  // ← Cache misses!
```

**GOOD: Row-wise cache locality (2-3x speedup)**
```chapel
// Best: Respect memory layout
for i in 0..#N do
  for j in 0..#N do
    C[i,j] += A[i,k] * B[k,j];  // ← Better cache!
```

**OPTIMAL: Cache-conscious tiling**
```chapel
const TILE_SIZE = 64;  // Fit in L1 cache (~32KB)

for ii in 0..#N by TILE_SIZE {
  for jj in 0..#N by TILE_SIZE {
    for kk in 0..#N by TILE_SIZE {

      // Process 64x64 tile in registers/L1
      for i in ii..#min(TILE_SIZE, N-ii) do
        for j in jj..#min(TILE_SIZE, N-jj) do
          for k in kk..#min(TILE_SIZE, N-kk) do
            C[i,j] += A[i,k] * B[k,j];
    }
  }
}

// Performance: 2-3x speedup vs naive sequential
```

