## 3. PARALLEL ITERATOR PATTERNS

🔍 **EXTRACTED FROM OFFICIAL DOCS**: Parallel Iterators Primer

### 3.1 Standalone Parallel Iterators

**Purpose**: Define parallelism for `forall` loops

```chapel
// Serial iterator (required baseline)
iter count(n: int, low: int = 1) {
  for i in low..#n do
    yield i;
}

// Parallel standalone iterator
iter count(param tag: iterKind, n: int, low: int = 1) 
  where tag == iterKind.standalone 
{
  config const numTasks = here.maxTaskPar;

  coforall tid in 0..#numTasks {
    const myIters = computeChunk(low..#n, tid, numTasks);
    for i in myIters do
      yield i;
  }
}

// Usage
forall i in count(1000000) do
  A[i] = expensive_computation(i);
```

**Performance**: Automatic work distribution across cores

### 3.2 Leader-Follower Iterators

**Purpose**: Enable zippered parallel loops with custom data structures

```chapel
// Leader: Partitions work and defines parallelism
iter count(param tag: iterKind, n: int, low: int = 1) 
  where tag == iterKind.leader 
{
  config const numTasks = here.maxTaskPar;

  coforall tid in 0..#numTasks {
    const myIters = computeChunk(low..#n, tid, numTasks);
    const zeroBasedIters = myIters.translate(-low);
    yield (zeroBasedIters,);  // Yield work chunk
  }
}

// Follower: Iterates over partition
iter count(param tag: iterKind, n: int, low: int = 1, followThis) 
  where tag == iterKind.follower 
{
  const (followInds,) = followThis;
  const lowBasedIters = followInds.translate(low);

  for i in lowBasedIters do
    yield i;  // Serially iterate
}

// Usage: Zippered iteration
forall (i, a) in zip(count(1000), A) do
  a = i / 10.0;
```

**Performance**: 
- Single-core: 90%+ efficiency
- Multi-core: Near-linear scaling

### 3.3 Advanced Iterator Pattern: Data + Model Parallelism

```chapel
// Combine data parallelism (batches) with model parallelism (layers)

iter neuralNetBatches(param tag: iterKind, 
                      numBatches: int, 
                      batchSize: int) 
  where tag == iterKind.standalone 
{
  const batchesPerTask = (numBatches + numTasks - 1) / numTasks;

  coforall tid in 0..#numTasks {
    const start = tid * batchesPerTask;
    const end = min((tid + 1) * batchesPerTask, numBatches);

    for batch in start..#(end - start) do
      yield batch;
  }
}

// Usage
forall batch in neuralNetBatches(numBatches, BATCH_SIZE) {
  var X = loadBatch(batch);  // Data parallelism

  // Model parallelism across layers
  for layer in 0..#numLayers {
    H = forwardLayer(layer, X);
    X = H;
  }
}
```

